+# 20261106-003
+
+## Purpose
+
+Translate the connected stage1 graph read/selection boundary through its actual UI callers, from existing Source45/PlusCal25, rather than adding polishing or compatibility infrastructure. Incremental unit over the pre-unit working tree, not a cumulative patch against HEAD. HEAD stays 28e6dc762c75c8a2ffbbe53ed08b323f0b2b82bd.
+
+## Actual changes and reasons
+
+- `sourcecode/backend/project_state.js`: implement declared graphs.readPalette/hasSelectedSlot/defaultColors and assets.readTree queries with immutable copies; restrict graph-data chart resolution to visible graph owners. Backend owns model meaning and complete CSV rows; defaults do not read project state.
+- `sourcecode/application/public_api/graphs.js`: return official graphs.readData/readPalette projections, pass explicit selection scalars, and route CSV path/object index intents through existing Adapter validation. Remove unused graphEditorChart/graphEditorCommit, direct live graph/CSV read assembly and redundant validation/notifications. No alternate mutation authority remains in those helpers.
+- `sourcecode/application/public_api/index.js`: bind assets.readTree and graph predicate/defaults to their specified queries, not direct model/config calculation or selected-slot truthiness.
+- `sourcecode/application/adapter.js`: use official Frontend readState for selection supplied to reference validation instead of internal interfaceRuntime alias; existing validation and dispatch remain owners.
+- `sourcecode/frontend/mantine_ui.js`: consume declared graph data/color sequence; obtain available CSV choices from asset tree, map selected option to canonical path, keep numeric object csvId intent, and slice preview rows only in presentation. No legacy-return-shape facade.
+- `agent_space/tests/browser-regression.js`: update existing24/64/168 only for actual contract changes and existing real read/selection paths, immutable values and graph-slot semantics. No new IDs/suites;167 historical cases remain, unexecuted.
+- `development-versions.json`: source-code131, stale, fingerprint sha256:b76090c94f3190e7737220658fa97f7815a684ffc4c299035bb20f0ba1cb4882 and this unit's review reference. Source45/PlusCal25/verification26 and lineage unchanged. Version validation is pending, not declared completed.
+- `agent_space/plans/plan-023.md` and `agent_space/reviews/review-20261106-003-graph-read-boundary-open.md`: record correspondence, scope, actual evidence and open stages.
+
+The Source public query/selection routes and Backend read contracts already specify these meanings; no upper-layer change/closure amendment is needed. UI render-local variables are not authority, copies are never mutation inputs here, and full snapshots are not retained. No new candidate, cache, task, retry or rollback semantics.
+
+## Alternatives rejected
+
+Keeping UI-shaped csv/csvOptions/palette compatibility output would duplicate the declared contract. Moving options/preview slicing to Backend would mix presentation with model meaning. Selecting current CSV from object.csvId or the asset option tree would replace the declared selection authority. A selected-slot truthiness check incorrectly accepts image slots; requiring a chart incorrectly rejects empty graph slots. Keeping live graph mutation helpers adds an alternative authority. Broad new mocked suites would displace translation work.
+
+## Evidence and limitations
+
+Static incremental file/diff/import-reference inspection and git whitespace checking only. Canonical LF git-blob hash calculation reproduced r130 29613ca0ba37bdb581e35d20541dbb94b661306ce80317e6a0c68c7f4ef554bc and yielded r131 b76090c94f3190e7737220658fa97f7815a684ffc4c299035bb20f0ba1cb4882; this is not the official checker. Raw CRLF checkout is not normalized. The numeric patch uses repository-normalized text and the pre-unit bytes of all eight existing changed files, saved temporarily within repository .git, plus the new review. The patch/explanation pair excludes itself. `git apply --reverse --check agent_space/patches/20261106-003.patch` and `git diff --check` completed successfully; these are static applicability/whitespace checks, not runtime verification. The temporary baseline was then removed.
+
+No application/test/build/checker/Actions/TLC execution, remote changes, commit, push or delegation. Official checker, runtime/React integration and inline/split behavior await authorized Actions. Prior r129 execution deviation is not evidence for this unit. Preserve original regression cleanup WIP/failure log/review and prior r129/r130 runtime/record changes; this patch does not roll them back or absorb them as newly implemented work. No access to previously denied .work/lifecycle-boundary-20261106/.
+
+Not done: whole graph-owner certification, remaining asset read/helper translation, whole stage1 completion, stage2 live capture/resource lifetime, stage3 remaining owners, stage4 integration. Code remains stale; safe implementation is not made conditional on a fabricated execution gate. Policies, upper layers and generated dist artifacts are unchanged.
