++# Graph reads and actual editor callers — translation review
++
++## Purpose and authority
++
++Continue plan-023 stage1 from Source45 → PlusCal25 → code across a connected responsibility boundary, rather than treating successful UI behavior as the criterion.
++
++- `sourcescript/backend/project_state.py` PUBLIC_BACKEND_READ_CONTRACTS (`graphs.readData`, `graphs.readPalette`, `graphs.hasSelectedSlot`, `graphs.defaultColors`, `assets.readTree`) and `pseudocode/backend/project_state.pcal` define Backend-owned detached reads. The existing graphs.readData calculation is reused, not reimplemented in Application. Its chart resolution now excludes hidden/non-graph slots, including explicit owner reads. Missing palette/graph-slot/default queries are translated; graph-slot presence deliberately does not require a chart. Default colors require no project read. Asset tree uses the existing pure calculation with explicit current project fields and immutable copy.
++- `sourcescript/application/public_api/__init__.py` and `pseudocode/application/public_api/contract.pcal` selected-query/query/select-asset/select-object routes control the public boundary. Graph readData passes only selectedSlotId/assetPath/assetSelection/graphObjectIndex; palette and hasSelectedSlot pass current selectedSlotId; defaultColors and assets.readTree simply query. No direct live chart/current-CSV model assembly remains in these reads.
++- Public graph CSV selection accepts canonical path, not a UI numeric-ID shortcut. Explicit object selection sends selectAsset=true through the Adapter's existing validation once. Source Adapter reference validation obtains current selection through official readState; the internal runtime alias is no longer imported by Adapter. Redundant public validation, extra notifications and unused graphEditorChart/graphEditorCommit are removed, not hidden behind a compatibility layer.
++- `sourcescript/frontend/mantine_ui.py` / `pseudocode/frontend/mantine_ui.pcal` retain UI responsibility for presentation and intent formation. The graph data/palette components now use the declared read shapes. CSV options derive from assets.readTree; UI maps selected option ID to canonical path, while object csvId mutation stays numeric. Thirty-row preview slicing happens only in the UI, not the public read. Palette eligibility uses detached chart data and its save uses the specified color sequence; no fabricated palette record is returned by Backend.
++
++No Source/PlusCal meaning was changed. All changed responsibilities already exist there; no Source amendment/closure change is needed. No new state, mirrors, retained read snapshots, candidate construction, retry/rollback, task owner or mutation path is introduced. Work-local UI values are presentation only.
++
++## Necessary existing coverage
++
++Case24 follows currentCsv/columns rather than the removed legacy csv.columns shape while retaining the distinction from objectColumns. Case64 now also exercises the real public CSV/object selection and immutable graph/palette/default/tree reads, and distinguishes hidden/image/empty-graph selections; it does not replace runtime owners with choreography mocks. Its existing fixture state restoration remains. Case168 recognizes the distinct official graphs.hasSelectedSlot query rather than requiring a slots.readSelected implementation shortcut. Cases/IDs remain167. No new test suite or IDs; authored assertions are not execution evidence.
