+# 20261106-004
+
+## Purpose and actual change
+
+Translate the connected asset-tree movement, drag and selection boundary from Source r45 / PlusCal r25. Public VFS reads no longer own movement eligibility, destination filtering, drag resolution or direct move-planning calls. Backend official queries calculate these from the current authoritative project. Directory/image selection invokes the specified single Adapter-validated asset event, rather than pre-clearing graph selection and reporting successful UI effects outside acceptance.
+
+Changed: `sourcecode/backend/project_state.js`, `sourcecode/application/public_api/assets.js`, `sourcecode/application/public_api/index.js`, existing regression112, `development-versions.json`, plan023 and review20261106-004. Backend also implements the declared resolveTreeSelection read with detached scalar output. Existing UI callers already consume movement path/kind and selection effects; no facade or UI state migration was added.
+
+## Reasons and rejected alternatives
+
+- Chose official queries because current source membership, fixed roots, canonical identities and destination rules belong to Backend. Reusing existing pure planProjectNodeMove with explicit current source avoids duplicating the move algorithm.
+- Rejected keeping Application destination filters: they allowed missing/fixed inputs and silently removed trash destinations contrary to the declared procedure.
+- Rejected preliminary CLEAR_GRAPH_OBJECT or a separate availability publication: SELECT_ASSET already owns accepted selection and graph-index clearing; wrong-kind references must not produce intermediate changes.
+- Rejected introducing a generic query facade, a cached asset-tree model or a compatibility return-shape bridge: direct routes suffice and temporary reads must not become authority.
+- Did not expand a test suite. Only existing112 was extended for the changed ownership paths. Execution remains pending, so assertions are not claimed to pass.
+
+## Recording and verification limits
+
+`20261106-004.patch` is the actual incremental diff from the working tree immediately before this unit, NOT a cumulative HEAD diff. Earlier original WIP and units001–003 are prerequisites and are not copied into this patch. The branch HEAD remains `28e6dc762c75c8a2ffbbe53ed08b323f0b2b82bd`; no commit/push or remote write was performed. Raw pre-unit bytes were recorded temporarily inside repository `.git/agent-unit-20261106-004.json` solely to create this incremental patch; that temporary baseline is removed after static patch checking. The patch includes the new review but excludes its own patch/explanation pair to avoid self-reference.
+
+Code revision132/stale records the LF-canonical source hash `sha256:96643e941e147d88e03cfb600af3fa31bd77f52e5644e3b9c048633110a54727`, after reproducing r131 from the recorded baseline. Upper-layer versions and derived_from remain unchanged. The hash calculation is a static file operation, not a version-checker execution or pass. Checkout line endings were not globally normalized.
+
+No application, test, build, checker, browser, TLC or Actions execution. Static incremental diff, whitespace and reverse patch applicability are the only verification surfaces used. Official version validation is pending authorized Actions; version work is not declared validated or complete.
+
+## Omissions and follow-up
+
+The Application readTrash summary and its confirmation UI, exact tree-projection correspondence, other asset reads/wrappers, whole stage1, capture/resource lifetimes and full integration remain open. This patch does not claim whole-owner completion or change Source/pseudocode to accommodate legacy code. No policy, dist, verification-model or unrelated cleanup changes. Prior WIP and failure evidence are preserved. The denied external `.work/lifecycle-boundary-20261106/` path was not accessed.
